<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Crowfoot</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1830–<a href="/years/1890">1890</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Isapo-Muxika</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Crowfoot was a chief of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siksika">Siksika</a>, one of the Blackfoot peoples of the northern plains. A noted warrior, he became a leading advocate of peace with the Canadian government as the bison disappeared, and he signed Treaty 7 in 1877, which ceded much of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alberta">Alberta</a>. He kept the Blackfoot out of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-west-rebellion">North-West Rebellion</a> of 1885.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/crowfoot.jpg" alt="Crowfoot" width="320" height="405" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alex Ross · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chief_Crowfoot.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
